text.section:
Each public institution of higher education shall meet the following financial and administrative management standards:

An unqualified opinion from the Auditor of Public Accounts upon the audit of the public institution's financial statements;


No significant audit deficiencies attested to by the Auditor of Public Accounts;


Substantial compliance with all financial reporting standards approved by the State Comptroller;


Substantial attainment of accounts receivable standards approved by the State Comptroller, including any standards for outstanding receivables and bad debts;


Substantial attainment of accounts payable standards approved by the State Comptroller including any standards for accounts payable past due; and


Other financial and administrative management standards established by the Governor or included in the general appropriation act currently in effect.
